# Open-source safety (mandatory)

This repo is **public**. Production is `app.penopta.com` on Vercel. Follow
[`docs/opensource-safety.md`](docs/opensource-safety.md) on every change.
If a task would violate it, **stop** — do not implement a workaround.

## Do not create or commit

- Secrets: `.env*` other than `.env.example`, tokens, DB URLs (except the
  local Docker example), OAuth secrets, `CRON_SECRET`, user maps
- Private maintainer files: anything under `docs/private/` except its README;
  do not add `docs/plans/`
- Citations of `docs/private/…` in tracked docs, comments, or logs
- Vercel team / `*.vercel.app` URLs, Neon hostnames, `.vercel/`
- `*.dmg` / installer zips / `Penopta-Sync.json` (Release assets only)
- Debug/admin/env-dump routes, auth bypasses, hardcoded fallback secrets

```ts
// Forbidden
const secret = process.env.CRON_SECRET || "dev-secret";

// Required
const secret = process.env.CRON_SECRET?.trim();
if (!secret) return new Response("Not configured.", { status: 500 });
```

## Do not weaken the live site

- Keep the app login-required; no public project list
- Keep org-scoped reads; do not authz org data by `owner_user_id` alone
- Cron stays Bearer `CRON_SECRET` and fails closed if unset
- `db:wipe` stays localhost-only / refuses Neon
- No Preview/stage env that reuses Production `DATABASE_URL` or OAuth secrets
- No `NEXT_PUBLIC_` or client imports for server secrets
- Logs and API errors stay generic — no tokens, cookies, or connection strings

Unpublished plans go in `docs/private/plans/` (local). Public durable docs go
in `docs/` (`architecture.md`, `opensource-safety.md`) and `AGENTS.md`.
